{%- comment -%}
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  theinmag-flip-callout
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  A "we did that on purpose" card for issues where the PRINT edition
  does something a buyer could mistake for a manufacturing fault.

  Built for Mag09, where printed pages 62 to 67 (the jokes, puzzles
  and riddles section, three double page spreads) are printed upside
  down deliberately so kids turn the magazine around. Customers were
  reporting it as a printing error, so we say it before they buy.

  The card is print-only by nature: the digital edition of Mag09 was
  corrected and reads the right way up. Do not reword this into
  something that implies the PDF is flipped too.

  WHY THE HEADING IS UPSIDE DOWN
  The heading is rotated 180deg in CSS so the card demonstrates the
  joke instead of describing it. The rotation is presentation only:
  DOM order is untouched, so screen readers and crawlers read it
  normally. Hovering un-rotates it as a desktop flourish; under
  prefers-reduced-motion the TRANSITION is removed but the flip still
  happens, which is correct (the rotation is the content, not an
  animation).

  There is deliberately NO tabindex here. An earlier version put
  tabindex="0" on the aside so keyboard users could un-rotate three
  words, which bought almost nothing and inserted a tab stop between
  the Format radiogroup and Add to cart. It also did not help the
  mobile majority, since :focus-visible does not match touch focus.
  The body copy underneath states the whole message the right way up,
  so the rotated heading is emphasis, not information.

  Keep the heading to three or four words. A rotated paragraph is a
  gag that stops being funny at line two.

  USAGE
    {% render 'theinmag-flip-callout', issue: issue %}

  Renders nothing unless the issue carries single_mag.flip_note, so
  it is safe to call for every issue in the picker loop.

  METAFIELDS (namespace: single_mag)
    flip_note     rich_text_field         REQUIRED, gates the card
    flip_heading  single_line_text_field  optional, defaults below
    flip_image    file_reference          optional photo of the real
                                          printed spread

  Spec: theinmag-docs/theinmag-design-system.md section 6 (callout
  archetype). Colour is the mint pair, chosen because it echoes the
  green ground of the actual printed section and because this is a
  kid-facing gag, not a warning. It is a light ground on a card
  surface, so it does not trip the adjacent-saturation rule.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign flip_note = issue.metafields.single_mag.flip_note
  assign flip_heading = issue.metafields.single_mag.flip_heading | default: 'upside down on purpose'
  assign flip_image = issue.metafields.single_mag.flip_image.value
-%}

{%- if flip_note != blank -%}
  <aside
    class="theinmag-flip-callout"
    data-flip-callout
    role="note"
    aria-label="A note about how this issue is printed"
  >
    <div class="theinmag-flip-callout__stamp" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false">
        <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7"/>
        <polyline points="3 4 3 9 8 9"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <p class="theinmag-flip-callout__heading">{{ flip_heading }}</p>

    <div class="theinmag-flip-callout__body">
      {{ flip_note | metafield_tag }}
    </div>

    {%- if flip_image != blank -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign flip_img_src = flip_image
        if flip_image.preview_image
          assign flip_img_src = flip_image.preview_image
        endif
        # Alt text follows the issue, not a hardcoded Mag09, because this
        # snippet is meant to be reused on any issue that pulls a stunt.
        assign flip_issue_name = issue.title | split: ' - ' | last | default: 'this issue'
        assign flip_img_alt = 'A copy of ' | append: flip_issue_name | append: ' open at the pages that are printed upside down on purpose'
      -%}
      <figure class="theinmag-flip-callout__figure">
        {{
          flip_img_src
          | image_url: width: 900
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            widths: '300, 450, 600, 900',
            sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 380px, 90vw',
            alt: flip_img_alt,
            class: 'theinmag-flip-callout__img'
        }}
      </figure>
    {%- endif -%}
  </aside>
{%- endif -%}
